PATCH 493: the damage roll b274 and its caller 9c76 -- the last remaining self-play crash (SAUDI3).

b274 (asm 0xb274-0xb2a1): bx is a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET into the per-weapon damage table (9c76 forms it as
0x9b5d + ax) and the roll is ((rand()&0xff) * byte[bx+1] >> 8) + byte[bx] + 1, scaled by word[0x9bae] --
or word[0x9bb0] when the current target word[0x9bb2] carries byte[+0x16] bit3 -- then >> 8.  Ghidra
deref'd bx as a host pointer.  9c76 (asm 0x9c76-0x9c96) is the per-type DAMAGE method c31e dispatches
with the object's NEAR offset as ARG0 (AX still holds the weapon index c31e stashed at word[0x9bdb]); it
adds the roll to byte[di+0x1a] and at 0x14 destroys the object and decrements word[0x930a].  Ghidra took
the object from param_2 -- a stale stack slot -- and deref'd it as a host pointer.
With this and patch 492 the 47-mission native self-play sweep has 46 missions running crash-free; the
remaining one is INDIA3, which never reaches the mission at all (board:0006 spawn OOM).
